def orow(p, r, verdict, prose): SO[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

orow(41, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY THE COMMANDMENTS BEFORE THEY CONQUERED AND SETTLED? THOSE AFTER — GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF, THE CORNER, TITHES, THE HEAVE-OFFERING, SABBATICAL YEARS AND JUBILEES — WHENCE? "IF YOU HEARKEN TO MY COMMANDMENTS" (11:13): TO ADD OTHER COMMANDMENTS TO THEM. The row on 11:13 ({SP_(41, 3, "לקט", "שכחה", "ופאה")} "gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"): THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF (24:19) named among the land\'s commandments learned after the settlement — the English\'s citation; the compile\'s daemon on the harvest\'s three gifts. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 11 and 15, deu_11_ekev_reeh and deu_15_reeh).')
orow(63, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'IF ONE FESTIVAL PASSED AND HE DID NOT BRING IT, DOES HE TRANSGRESS "DELAY NOT"? "THESE YOU SHALL DO TO THE LORD AT YOUR APPOINTED TIMES" (Numbers 29:39) — HE DOES NOT TRANSGRESS "DELAY NOT" UNTIL THE FESTIVALS OF A WHOLE YEAR PASS OVER HIM. The row on 12:5 ({SP_(63, 5, "בל", "תאחר")} "delay not"): THE VOW\'S CLOCK — 23:22\'s "delay not to pay it" measured by the three festivals (Rosh Hashanah 1:1 the answer sheet); the compile\'s clock parameter for chapter 23. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12, deu_12_reeh).')
orow(87, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM "FATHERS SHALL NOT BE PUT TO DEATH FOR SONS" (24:16) WE LEARNED THAT THEY DO NOT TESTIFY FOR ONE ANOTHER; AS THEY DO NOT TESTIFY, DO THEY NOT INCITE ONE ANOTHER? "IF YOUR BROTHER, YOUR MOTHER\'S SON, INCITES YOU" (13:7). The row on 13:7 ({SP_(87, 3, "שאין", "מעידים", "זה", "לזה")} "that they do not testify for one another"): 24:16 READ AS THE KINSMEN\'S TESTIMONY — the fathers-and-sons verse the ground that relatives cannot witness (Sanhedrin 3:4 the answer sheet), the compile\'s witness parameter for chapter 24 already cited at the seducer. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13, deu_13_reeh).')
orow(94, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'HENCE: THE CHILDREN OF THE CONDEMNED CITY ARE NOT SPARED; ABBA HANAN SAYS: "FATHERS SHALL NOT BE PUT TO DEATH FOR SONS" (24:16) — OF THE CONDEMNED CITY THE VERSE SPEAKS; "THE INHABITANTS OF THAT CITY" — NOT ANOTHER CITY\'S; THE ASS-TRAIN AND THE CAMEL-TRAIN PASSING THROUGH SAVE IT; "BY THE SWORD\'S EDGE" — NOT TO DISFIGURE THEM. The row on 13:16 ({SP_(94, 3, "בעיר", "הנדחת", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of the condemned city the verse speaks"): Abba Hanan\'s reading of 24:16 as the condemned city\'s children (against the row\'s first ruling) — a second seat of the verse in chapter 13. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13, deu_13_reeh).')
orow(110, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE SOJOURNER, THE ORPHAN AND THE WIDOW IN YOUR GATES" (14:29) — NEEDY OR NOT? DO NOT WONDER: "TAKE NOT A WIDOW\'S GARMENT IN PLEDGE" (24:17) — POOR OR RICH! "THE POOR" (Leviticus 19:10) — AS THE POOR MAN IS NEEDY, SO ALL THESE. The row on 14:29 ({SP_(110, 1, "בין", "עניה", "ובין", "עשירה")} "whether poor or rich"): 24:17\'s WIDOW RICH OR POOR — the pledge\'s bar not conditioned on need, against the tithe\'s widow who must be needy; the compile\'s predicate for 24:17. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 14, deu_14_reeh).')
orow(117, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE CRIES AGAINST YOU TO THE LORD" (15:9) — A COMMANDMENT NOT TO CRY? "HE CRIES"; A COMMANDMENT TO CRY? "HE SHALL NOT CRY AGAINST YOU" (24:15); SIN ONLY IF HE CRIES? "IT SHALL BE SIN IN YOU" ANYWAY; WHY "HE CRIES"? I HASTEN TO REPAY THROUGH THE CRIER MORE THAN THROUGH THE SILENT. The row on 15:9 ({SP_(117, 5, "ממהר", "אני", "לפרע")} "I hasten to repay"): 24:15\'S CRY read with 15:9\'s — the hireling\'s and the needy\'s one heaven entry, the sin regardless, the cry the speed (the ink\'s find 7). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 15, deu_15_reeh).')
orow(122, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU TAKE THE AWL" (15:17) — THE THORN, THE GLASS, THE REED: "YOU TAKE", R. YOSE B. R. JUDAH; RABBI: THE AWL — METAL; HENCE R. ISHMAEL: IN THREE PLACES THE LAW GOES AROUND SCRIPTURE — "COVER IT WITH DUST" (Leviticus 17:13), THE LAW: ANYTHING THAT GROWS PLANTS; "HE WRITES HER A BILL OF CUTTING-OFF" (24:1), THE LAW: ON ANYTHING DETACHED; "WITH THE AWL", THE LAW: WITH ANYTHING; RABBI: STANDING. The row on 15:17 ({SP_(122, 1, "בשלשה", "מקומות", "הלכה", "עוקפת", "המקרא")} "in three places the law goes around Scripture"; {SP_(122, 1, "בכל", "דבר", "שהוא", "בתלוש")} "on anything that is detached"): THE BILL\'S MATERIAL — 24:1\'s "bill" widened by the law to anything detached from the ground (Gittin 2:4 the answer sheet): one of R. Ishmael\'s three; the compile\'s parameter on the divorce\'s writing. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 15, deu_15_reeh).')
orow(155, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND PURGE THE EVIL FROM ISRAEL" (17:12) — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. The row on 17:12 ({SP_(155, 9, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): the formula\'s third seat read as persons — 240:5 and 241:7 its words in chapter 22; the row sits among this ledger\'s outside rows by the translator\'s footnote alone ("Dt.22:1" for the formula\'s later seats), the Hebrew citing 17:12. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 17-18, deu_17_18_shoftim).')
orow(190, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT THE SHAMER PAYS MONEY? "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" HERE (19:21) AND "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" THERE (25:12): AS THERE MONEY, SO HERE MONEY. The row on 19:17 ({SP_(190, 14, "שהמביש", "משלם", "ממון")} "that the shamer pays money"): 25:12\'S "CUT OFF HER HAND" IS MONEY — the pity formula\'s analogy (I2) between the talion and the wrestler\'s wife: the compile\'s operator for chapter 25 (Bava Kamma 8:1 the answer sheet), read already at the talion. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 19-21, deu_19_21_shoftim_ki_teitzei).')
orow(336, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BY THIS THING YOU SHALL PROLONG DAYS" (32:47) — ONE OF THE THINGS WHOSE DOER EATS THEIR FRUIT IN THIS WORLD AND HAS LENGTH OF DAYS IN THE WORLD TO COME: HERE THE STUDY OF TORAH; HONORING FATHER AND MOTHER — "THAT YOUR DAYS BE LONG" (Exodus 20:12); SENDING THE NEST — "SURELY SEND THE MOTHER … THAT YOUR DAYS BE LONG" (22:7); BRINGING PEACE — "GREAT PEACE FOR YOUR CHILDREN" (Isaiah 54:13). The row on 32:47 ({SP_(336, 2, "בשלוח", "הקן", "כתוב")} "of the sending of the nest it is written"): THE NEST\'S REWARD in the list of Peah 1:1 with the parents\' and peace\'s — 22:7\'s clause the ground; a heaven entry\'s formula. Fresh.')
orow(352, 8, 'EXCLUDED', f'"AND BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS HE DWELLS" (33:12) — WHETHER IN RUIN OR NOT IN RUIN; SO "ALL THE KINGDOMS OF THE EARTH THE LORD GOD OF HEAVEN GAVE ME" (2 Chronicles 36:23). The row on 33:11-12 ({SP_(352, 8, "בין", "חרב", "בין", "שאינו", "חרב")} "whether in ruin or not in ruin"): the Temple\'s place holy in ruin — THE ENGLISH CITES "Dt.23:12" FOR THE BLESSING OF BENJAMIN\'S 33:12, a misprint; the Hebrew cites no verse of chapter 23: EXCLUDED from this ledger\'s coverage, read whole. Fresh.')
orow(352, 9, 'EXCLUDED', f'ANOTHER WORD: "BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS HE DWELLS" — AS THE OX HAS NOTHING HIGHER THAN ITS SHOULDERS, SO THE TEMPLE IS HIGHER THAN ALL THE WORLD: "YOU SHALL ARISE AND GO UP TO THE PLACE" (17:8), "MANY PEOPLES SHALL GO: COME, LET US GO UP" (Isaiah 2:3) — NOT GAD FROM THE EAST AND DAN FROM THE WEST, BUT "MANY PEOPLES". The row on 33:11-12 ({SP_(352, 9, "גבוה", "מכל", "העולם")} "higher than all the world"): the Temple\'s height from 17:8\'s "go up" — the English\'s "Dt.23:12" the same misprint: EXCLUDED from this ledger\'s coverage. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 17-18, deu_17_18_shoftim).')
orow(352, 10, 'EXCLUDED', f'RABBI SAYS: OF EVERY BORDER IT SAYS "THE BORDER WENT DOWN", "WAS DRAWN", AND HERE "THE BORDER WENT UP THE VALLEY OF BEN-HINNOM TO THE SHOULDER OF THE JEBUSITE ON THE SOUTH — JERUSALEM" (Joshua 15:8): THE CHOSEN HOUSE WAS BUILT IN BENJAMIN\'S PORTION; R. MEIR: IN BENJAMIN\'S, AND A STRIP WENT OUT INTO JUDAH\'S — "BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS"; "THE SCEPTER SHALL NOT DEPART FROM JUDAH" (Genesis 49:10) — THE CHAMBER OF HEWN STONE IN JUDAH\'S; THE GREAT HOUSE IN JOSEPH\'S AT SHILOH; [R. JUDAH: IN JUDAH\'S,] "BETHLEHEM EPHRATAH" (Micah 5:1), EPHRATH IS BETHLEHEM (Genesis 35:19). The row on 33:11-12 ({SP_(352, 10, "בחלקו", "של", "בנימין")} "in Benjamin\'s portion"): the Temple\'s tribe — the English\'s "Dt.23:12" the misprint: EXCLUDED from this ledger\'s coverage, read whole. Fresh.')
orow(352, 17, 'EXCLUDED', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHY DID BENJAMIN MERIT THE PRESENCE IN HIS PORTION? A KING WITH MANY SONS — EACH GROWN SEIZED HIS PLACE; THE YOUNGEST HIS FATHER LOVED, ATE AND DRANK WITH HIM, LEANED ON HIM GOING OUT AND COMING IN; SO BENJAMIN THE RIGHTEOUS, THE YOUNGEST OF THE TRIBES, ON WHOM JACOB LEANED: WHERE THIS RIGHTEOUS ONE LEANED HIS HANDS, THERE I SET MY PRESENCE — "BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS HE DWELLS". The row on 33:11-12 ({SP_(352, 17, "קטן", "שבשבטים", "היה")} "he was the youngest of the tribes"): the parable of the leaning father — the English\'s "Dt.23:12" the misprint: EXCLUDED from this ledger\'s coverage, read whole. Fresh.')
